# This repo deliberately does NOT use Git LFS.
#
# It used to route *.csv (plus *.tif/*.tiff/*.shp/*.shx/*.dbf/*.geojson/*.gpkg)
# through LFS, but the only files that ever matched were the four small text
# CSVs in Data/ (177 KB together). They are now stored in regular git.
#
# The cost of that blanket rule was a hard dependency on LFS in every CI
# checkout: when the org's Git LFS budget was exhausted on 2026-08-16, the
# `git lfs fetch` in actions/checkout failed and took down both the PR preview
# and the main dashboard build, over 177 KB of plain text.
#
# Large binary data belongs in the sibling repo INRB-UMIE/BDBV2026-Data, which
# uses LFS deliberately and scopes it to data/*/raw/** so that nothing needed
# at clone time (build/, data/*/processed/, data/shapefiles/) sits behind it.
# If a genuinely large binary ever has to live here, add a narrow rule for that
# path -- and remember it makes this repo's CI depend on LFS again.
